statement:
Let $k \ge 1$, and let $f : \mathbb{Z}_k^n \to \mathbb{Z}_k$. For each $j \in \mathbb{Z}_k$ let $\widetilde{f}_j(x) = \omega_k^{\,j\,f(x)}$ denote the $j$-twisted lift of $f$, and write $\widehat{\widetilde{f}_j}(s)$ for its Fourier coefficient at frequency $s \in \mathbb{Z}_k^n$. Then the BLR acceptance probability of $f$ admits the representation
\[
  \Pr_{x,y}\bigl[f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y)\bigr]
  = \frac{1}{k}
    \sum_{j\in\mathbb{Z}_k}\;
    \sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_k^n}
    \bigl|\widehat{\widetilde{f}_j}(s)\bigr|^2\,
    \operatorname{Re}\widehat{\widetilde{f}_j}(s),
\]
where $|\cdot|$ is the complex modulus and $\operatorname{Re}$ the real part.

